    "text": "Total number of isomers (including stereoisomers) obtain on monochlorination of methylcyclohexane is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ddf9c7e9-af47-45d3-8d39-99c923ae2175-9-8-2022NEW.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Compound A&nbsp;and B&nbsp;given above have&nbsp;no chiral centre and doesn&#39;t show geometrical isomerism.</p><p>Compound C&nbsp;and D&nbsp;given above have&nbsp;two&nbsp;chiral centres each and each of them forms 4 optical isomers.</p><p>And compound E&nbsp;has 2&nbsp;E and Z isomers due to restricted rotation of groups.</p><p>Hence, the total number of&nbsp; isomers will be 12.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
